WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.207 line:92%
-Hey, Jimmy, quick question.

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you know about
Puerto Rico?

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.612 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Puerto Rico? Not much.

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I know it's
an unincorporated territory

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.618
of the United States, about
1,000 miles southeast of Miami.

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know it's known locally
as Borinquen,

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the indigenous Taino name
Borinken,

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
meaning
"land of the valiant Lord."

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, and it was
colonized by Spain in 1493

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.564 line:92%
after the arrival of Columbus,

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and remained in
Spanish possession

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:34.067 line:92%
for the next four centuries.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:37.704
And the U.S. acquired it in 1898
after the Spanish-American War

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
under the terms of
the Treaty of Paris.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:41.341 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And its political status

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been a matter of
public debate ever since.

00:00:43.276 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, but --
-Oh, and its chief exports

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
include rum and electronics
and pharmaceuticals

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
and chemicals
and medical equipment.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't believe
I forgot medical equipment,

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:56.756 line:92%
and, of course, canned tuna.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
Other than that, I don't know
much about Puerto Rico.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Why?

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:04.764
-"Hamilton" is playing in
Puerto Rico and we got tickets.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.666 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Want to come?

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wepa!

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:13.540 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-From the beautiful island of
Puerto Rico,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:19.279 size:84% position:42%
it's "The Tonight Show"
starring Jimmy Fallon!

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.916
Tonight, join Jimmy and his
guests Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:27.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
the cast of "Hamilton,"
Bad Bunny, Chef Jose Andres,

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
and music from
Jose Feliciano and Ozuna.

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:36.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now here's your host --
Jimmy Fallon!

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:37.697 line:92%
-Hola, everyone. We're here.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.833 size:88% position:44%
We are so excited to be
doing "The Tonight Show"

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the beautiful island of
Puerto Rico.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.203 line:92%
Even just walking around,

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can feel the energy
and the spirit of this place.

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:48.208 size:81% position:41%
The history, the food,
the music, the people,

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:50.944
Puerto Rico is thriving,
and it's open for business.

00:01:50.944 --> 00:01:53.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what better way to show it
than Lin-Manuel Miranda

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:56.416
taking his whole team on
the road and bringing "Hamilton"

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Puerto Rico
for the very first time?

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.653 line:92%
They're supporting the arts.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're raising money
for the island,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:05.058 size:84% position:42%
and they're celebrating
all the amazing things

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.459 line:92%
Puerto Rico has to offer.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when we heard that Lin was
doing that, we were like,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're coming down too,
and we're ready to party."

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
So now we're here.
We're in San Juan.

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're outside
the "Hamilton" theater.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.904
I was gonna go watch the show,
but then I thought to myself,

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:18.905 line:92%
"Why just watch 'Hamilton'

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:23.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I can actually
be in 'Hamilton?'" Here we go.

